Allow a frontend to pair two Gambatte instances over loopback.

The ordinary network slave must poll without blocking, but a local paired
instance can briefly wait for its concurrently-running master. This rendezvous
prevents the slave from finishing a frame just before the master posts its
byte, which would otherwise leave the master blocked until the next frontend
frame. "Local Server" and "Local Client" are intentionally internal option
values; they need not appear in RetroArch's option list.

